  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nThe western upper ridge will remain fairly flat through midweek\nwith a series of weak shortwaves pushing along the international\nborder. This will keep temperatures slightly below normal and\nbring scattered showers and a few thunderstorms into Montana. The\ntiming of the waves indicate late afternoon to overnight\nprecipitation. \n\nUpper ridge builds into the area for Wednesday, Thursday and \nFriday with a return to warmer and drier conditions for the end of\nthe week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nMain deviations to the NBM were to spread pops across a larger\narea for Sunday night through Monday night.",
